An oxygen separator for generating an oxygen-enriched gas from an oxygen-comprising gas, said oxygen separator comprising:

a) an oxygen separator device comprising:
   i) a sorbent material configured to sorb at least one component of the oxygen-comprising gas; and
   ii) at least two controllable interfaces, comprising a first controllable interface and a second controllable interface, configured to control the communication of gas between the interior and exterior of the oxygen separator device;

b) a processor configured to control the oxygen separator such that a plurality of phases are carried out sequentially, including a purging phase;

wherein the processor is configured to control the at least two controllable interfaces so as to generate a flow of gas between the first controllable interface and the second controllable interface during at least the purging phase, and wherein the second controllable interface is positioned and/or controlled such that it governs the fluidic coupling between the interior of the oxygen separator device and a volume of non-oxygen-enriched gas during the purging phase.

