# Patent Claim - Oxygen Generator with Adsorption Technology

## Claim 1

An oxygen generator system comprising:

a) at least one adsorption bed containing a molecular sieve material configured to selectively adsorb nitrogen from a compressed air feed stream, thereby producing an oxygen-enriched product gas via a pressure swing adsorption process;

b) a compressor operatively coupled to the at least one adsorption bed, configured to deliver the compressed air feed stream at a predetermined pressure range;

c) a first controllable gas interface disposed at an inlet region of the at least one adsorption bed, configured to selectively regulate flow of the compressed air feed stream into the adsorption bed, wherein said first controllable gas interface comprises a first solenoid valve operatively controlled by a processor;

d) a second controllable gas interface disposed at an outlet region of the at least one adsorption bed, configured to selectively regulate flow of the oxygen-enriched product gas from the adsorption bed to a product gas outlet, wherein said second controllable gas interface comprises a second solenoid valve operatively controlled by the processor, said second controllable gas interface being independently actuable relative to the first controllable gas interface;

e) a purge conduit fluidly coupled between the at least one adsorption bed and a purge valve, wherein the purge valve is operatively controlled by the processor;

f) the processor being configured to execute a purge cycle comprising:
   (i) monitoring a pressure parameter, a timing parameter, or both, associated with an adsorption phase of the at least one adsorption bed;
   (ii) upon satisfaction of a predetermined threshold condition, actuating the first controllable gas interface to a closed position to terminate the flow of the compressed air feed stream into the adsorption bed;
   (iii) actuating the purge valve to an open position to release a purge gas flow from the at least one adsorption bed, thereby desorbing adsorbed nitrogen from the molecular sieve material; and
   (iv) actuating the purge valve to a closed position upon completion of a predetermined purge duration or upon detection of a predetermined pressure equalization condition, and subsequently re-actuating the first controllable gas interface to an open position to reinitiate the adsorption phase;

wherein the processor is further configured to coordinate actuation timing of the first controllable gas interface, the second controllable gas interface, and the purge valve to maintain a substantially continuous supply of the oxygen-enriched product gas at the product gas outlet.

---

## Dependent Claims (Optional Extensions)

**Claim 2:** The oxygen generator system of claim 1, wherein the at least one adsorption bed comprises a plurality of adsorption beds arranged in parallel, and wherein the processor is configured to alternate the purge cycle between the plurality of adsorption beds such that while a first adsorption bed undergoes the purge cycle, a second adsorption bed concurrently produces the oxygen-enriched product gas.

**Claim 3:** The oxygen generator system of claim 1, further comprising a pressure sensor operatively coupled to the processor and disposed to measure pressure within the at least one adsorption bed, wherein the predetermined threshold condition of step (ii) is determined based at least in part on a signal received from the pressure sensor.

**Claim 4:** The oxygen generator system of claim 1, further comprising an oxygen concentration sensor disposed at the product gas outlet and operatively coupled to the processor, wherein the processor is configured to adjust a duration of the purge cycle based on a signal received from the oxygen concentration sensor.

**Claim 5:** The oxygen generator system of claim 1, wherein the processor comprises a non-transitory computer-readable memory storing instructions for executing the purge cycle, and a timer module configured to track the predetermined purge duration.

**Claim 6:** The oxygen generator system of claim 1, wherein the second controllable gas interface further comprises a check valve configured to prevent backflow of the oxygen-enriched product gas into the at least one adsorption bed during the purge cycle.

# Patent Claim

**Claim 1:** An apparatus for separating oxygen from air, the apparatus comprising:

a housing defining an interior chamber;

a sorbent material disposed within the interior chamber, the sorbent material configured to selectively adsorb nitrogen from air passed therethrough, thereby producing an oxygen-enriched gas stream;

a first valve in fluid communication with the interior chamber, the first valve configured to control introduction of a feed gas into the interior chamber;

a second valve in fluid communication with the interior chamber, the second valve configured to control release of a waste gas from the interior chamber during a purge phase;

a processor operatively coupled to the first valve and the second valve, the processor configured to:

(a) actuate the first valve to a closed position at an initiation of the purge phase, thereby preventing further introduction of the feed gas into the interior chamber;

(b) actuate the second valve to an open position during the purge phase to permit release of the waste gas from the interior chamber, thereby facilitating desorption of nitrogen from the sorbent material; and

(c) actuate the second valve to a closed position and the first valve to an open position upon completion of the purge phase, thereby transitioning the apparatus to a subsequent phase of operation;

wherein the processor controls a duration of the purge phase based on at least one operational parameter of the apparatus.

---

**Claim 2** *(dependent):* The apparatus of claim 1, wherein the sorbent material comprises a zeolite material configured to selectively adsorb nitrogen under a first pressure condition and to release nitrogen under a second pressure condition lower than the first pressure condition.

**Claim 3** *(dependent):* The apparatus of claim 1, further comprising a pressure sensor in communication with the processor, wherein the processor determines the duration of the purge phase based at least in part on a pressure signal received from the pressure sensor.

**Claim 4** *(dependent):* The apparatus of claim 1, wherein the first valve and the second valve are solenoid valves electrically coupled to the processor.

**Claim 5** *(dependent):* The apparatus of claim 1, further comprising an oxygen outlet in fluid communication with the interior chamber, the oxygen outlet configured to deliver the oxygen-enriched gas stream to a downstream device.

